@namespace DotNetCloud.Modules.Contacts.UI

@*
    Help content for the Contacts module.
    Based on docs/user/CONTACTS.md.
*@

<div class="help-content">
    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Overview</h2>
        <p>DotNetCloud Contacts lets you store and manage your contacts, organize them into groups, share them with other users, and sync with external applications via CardDAV.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Managing Contacts</h2>
        <p><strong>Creating a contact:</strong> Click the <strong>+</strong> button in the sidebar header and fill in the details: display name (required), first and last name, organization, job title, primary email, and primary phone.</p>
        <p><strong>Editing:</strong> Click a contact to open it, click <strong>Edit Contact</strong>, change any fields, and click <strong>Save</strong>.</p>
        <p><strong>Deleting:</strong> Open a contact, click <strong>Edit Contact</strong>, then <strong>Delete</strong>. Contacts are soft-deleted.</p>
        <p><strong>Searching:</strong> Type in the search box in the sidebar and click <strong>Search</strong> to find contacts by name, email, phone, or organization.</p>
        <p><strong>Recently added:</strong> Use the <strong>Recently Added</strong> section in the sidebar to view your newest contacts.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Contact Groups</h2>
        <p>Groups are listed in the <strong>Groups</strong> section of the sidebar, showing each group's member count. Group management is not currently available in the web UI.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Sharing Contacts</h2>
        <p>Open a contact and click <strong>Share</strong> to share it with another user. Enter the recipient's user ID and choose whether they can <strong>Read Only</strong> view or <strong>Read/Write</strong> edit the shared contact. You can revoke a share at any time.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">CardDAV Sync</h2>
        <p>Contacts are accessible via CardDAV, allowing sync with external applications like Thunderbird, Apple Contacts, or mobile devices. Use your DotNetCloud credentials to connect.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Tips &amp; Tricks</h2>
        <ul class="help-tips">
            <li>Use groups to organize contacts by project, team, or relationship.</li>
            <li>Add multiple email addresses and phone numbers with different labels for flexibility.</li>
            <li>Use the search bar for quick access — it searches across all contact fields.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>
